// Unicode simple case mapping (one character for one), for
// `char::to_lowercase` and `char::to_uppercase`.
//
// The table covers the cased letters of Latin (with Extended-A to -D and
// Additional), Greek (with most of Extended), Cyrillic (with Extended-B),
// Armenian, Georgian (with Mtavruli), Cherokee, Glagolitic, Coptic, the
// letterlike symbols, Roman numerals, circled and fullwidth Latin
// letters, Deseret, Osage, Old Hungarian, Warang Citi, Medefaidrin and
// Adlam. Characters it does not list map to themselves, and so do
// lowercase letters whose uppercase is more than one character (`ß`).

/// Ranges of uppercase letters: `(first, last, delta, kind)`. Kind 0:
/// every letter in the range has its lowercase `delta` code points on.
/// Kind 1: the range alternates uppercase, lowercase, ..., starting with
/// `first`, and each lowercase letter follows its uppercase one. Earlier
/// entries win where the reverse mappings overlap.
static CASES: [(u32, u32, i32, u32); 151] = [
    (0x41, 0x5A, 32, 0),
    (0xC0, 0xD6, 32, 0),
    (0xD8, 0xDE, 32, 0),
    (0x100, 0x12E, 1, 1),
    (0x132, 0x136, 1, 1),
    (0x139, 0x147, 1, 1),
